"...         return G * self.mass / (self.radius * self.radius)\n"
"...\n"
">>> Planet.EARTH.value\n"
"(5.976e+24, 6378140.0)\n"
">>> Planet.EARTH.surface_gravity\n"
"9.802652743337129"

#: ../../howto/enum.rst:1479
msgid "TimePeriod"
msgstr "TimePeriod"

#: ../../howto/enum.rst:1481
msgid "An example to show the :attr:`~Enum._ignore_` attribute in use::"
msgstr ""
"Ein Beispiel, das das Attribut :attr:`~Enum._ignore_` im Einsatz zeigt::"

#: ../../howto/enum.rst:1483
msgid ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> class Period(dt.timedelta, Enum):\n"
"...     \"different lengths of time\"\n"
"...     _ignore_ = 'Period i'\n"
"...     Period = vars()\n"
"...     for i in range(367):\n"
"...         Period['day_%d' % i] = i\n"
"...\n"
">>> list(Period)[:2]\n"
"[<Period.day_0: datetime.timedelta(0)>, <Period.day_1: "
"datetime.timedelta(days=1)>]\n"
">>> list(Period)[-2:]\n"
"[<Period.day_365: datetime.timedelta(days=365)>, <Period.day_366: "
"datetime.timedelta(days=366)>]"
msgstr ""
">>> import datetime as dt\n"
">>> class Period(dt.timedelta, Enum):\n"
"...     \"different lengths of time\"\n"
"...     _ignore_ = 'Period i'\n"
"...     Period = vars()\n"
"...     for i in range(367):\n"
"...         Period['day_%d' % i] = i\n"
"...\n"
">>> list(Period)[:2]\n"
"[<Period.day_0: datetime.timedelta(0)>, <Period.day_1: "
"datetime.timedelta(days=1)>]\n"
">>> list(Period)[-2:]\n"
"[<Period.day_365: datetime.timedelta(days=365)>, <Period.day_366: "
"datetime.timedelta(days=366)>]"

#: ../../howto/enum.rst:1500
msgid "Subclassing EnumType"
msgstr "Von EnumType ableiten"

#: ../../howto/enum.rst:1502
msgid ""
"While most enum needs can be met by customizing :class:`Enum` subclasses, "
"either with class decorators or custom functions, :class:`EnumType` can be "
"subclassed to provide a different Enum experience."
msgstr ""
"Die meisten Bedürfnisse rund um Enums lassen sich dadurch erfüllen, dass "
"man :class:`Enum`-Unterklassen anpasst – entweder mit Klassendekoratoren "
"oder mit eigenen Funktionen. Es ist aber möglich, von :class:`EnumType` "
"abzuleiten, um ein anderes Enum-Erlebnis zu bieten."
